---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
import { log, questions } from '../data';
import metrics from '../metrics.json';
import ludo from '../assets/ludo.png';
import jutpatti from '../assets/jutpatti.png';

const notes = (await getCollection('notes')).sort((a, b) => +b.data.date - +a.data.date);
const m = metrics as Partial<Record<'measured' | 'js' | 'page' | 'fonts' | 'images', string>>;
const fmt = (d: string | Date) =>
  new Date(d).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'short', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });

const cifar = [
  { name: 'Random Forest', acc: 43.74 },
  { name: 'KNN', acc: 36.25 },
  { name: 'Gaussian NB', acc: 31.22 },
  { name: 'Decision Tree', acc: 25.62 },
  { name: 'CNN (teammate)', acc: 85.4, them: true },
];
const shot = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [280, 420, 560], sizes: '(min-width: 42rem) 19rem, 46vw', loading: 'lazy' as const };

const jsonld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: site.name,
  url: site.url,
  sameAs: [site.github],
  affiliation: { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: 'Tribhuvan University' },
};
---
<Base jsonld={jsonld}>
  <h1>Ronaz Pradhan</h1>
  <p>
    I study Computer Science and IT at Tribhuvan University in Nepal (4th semester, graduating 2028).
    I build web products, and I'm learning machine learning the same way: by building something and then
    measuring whether it actually works.
  </p>
  <p>
    Right now that means online Ludo and Jutpatti you can play with friends without ads or coin shops.
    Before that, a CIFAR-10 comparison of classical models for a university AI course.
  </p>
  <p class="small muted">
    <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a>{site.email && <> · <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></>}
  </p>

  <h2 id="projects">Projects</h2>

  <section class="project" aria-labelledby="p-games">
    <h3 id="p-games"><a href="/work/ludo">Ludo</a> and <a href="/work/jutpatti">Jutpatti</a></h3>
    <p class="stack">Node.js · ws · vanilla JS · 51 tests</p>
    <p>
      Two multiplayer games on one small Node server. Ludo lets the browsers run the game and the server relays
      moves. Jutpatti can't work that way, because a card game has hidden hands, so the server deals, holds every
      hand, and sends each player only their own cards.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <div class="shots">
        <Picture src={ludo} alt="Ludo board on a phone: four coloured home areas, one human player against three computer players." {...shot} />
        <Picture src={jutpatti} alt="Jutpatti table on a phone: my seven cards along the bottom, the opponent shown only as a name and a card count of 7." {...shot} />
      </div>
      <figcaption>Both running locally, captured at phone size. On the right, the other player is just “Aarav · 7”: the browser never receives their cards.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>This is the function that decides what each player is allowed to see (trimmed, from <code>games/jutpatti/engine.js</code>). Opponents become a count; someone else's draw shows its card only if it came off the discard pile, which everyone saw anyway.</p>
    <pre><code>{`players: state.players.map(p => ({ pid: p, cards: state.hands[p].length, active: ... })),
// ...
if (ld) v.lastDraw = { pid: ld.pid, source: ld.source,
  card: ld.source === 'discard' || ld.pid === pid ? ld.card : null };
if (mine && state.active.includes(pid)) {
  v.you = { hand: mine.slice(), validMoves: getValidMoves(state, pid) };
}`}</code></pre>
    <p class="small"><a href="/work/jutpatti">Jutpatti write-up</a> · <a href="/work/ludo">Ludo write-up</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ronazpradhan/ludo3d">Source</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="project" aria-labelledby="p-cifar">
    <h3 id="p-cifar"><a href="/work/cifar-10">CIFAR-10: classical ML against a CNN</a></h3>
    <p class="stack">Python · scikit-learn · PCA · Colab</p>
    <p>
      A two-person course project. I did the classical side: standardise, PCA down to 95% of the variance, then four
      models with different assumptions. Test accuracy on 10 classes (chance is 10%):
    </p>
    <ul class="bars" aria-label="Test accuracy by model">
      {cifar.map((r) => (
        <li class={r.them ? 'them' : undefined}>
          <span>{r.name}</span>
          <span class="bar" style={`--w:${r.acc}%`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="n">{r.acc.toFixed(2)}%</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="small muted">Dashed: my teammate Aakriti Maharjan's CNN, for comparison. Flattening an image throws away which pixels are neighbours; that gap is mostly the representation, not the model.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="project" aria-labelledby="p-money">
    <h3 id="p-money"><a href="https://github.com/ronazpradhan/money-tracker-web">Money Tracker</a></h3>
    <p class="stack">React Native · Expo · SQLite</p>
    <p>An offline-first Android app for logging income and expenses. Data stays on the phone, no account needed. The app source is private while I work on it; the link goes to its public page.</p>
  </section>

  <h2 id="questions">Open questions</h2>
  <p>Things I want to find out, rather than things I've finished.</p>
  <ul>
    {questions.map((x) => (
      <li>{x.q} <span class="muted">{x.href ? <a href={x.href}>{x.a}</a> : x.a}</span></li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 id="notes">Notes</h2>
  <p>Short write-ups of decisions, mostly about this site and the games.</p>
  <ul class="dated">
    {notes.map((n) => (
      <li><time datetime={n.data.date.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>{fmt(n.data.date)}</time><a href={`/notes/${n.id}`}>{n.data.title}</a></li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 id="changelog">Changelog</h2>
  <ul class="dated small">
    {log.map((l) => (
      <li><time datetime={l.date}>{fmt(l.date)}</time><span>{l.text}</span></li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p slot="foot" style="margin:0 0 0.5rem">
    This page: {m.page ?? '?'} of HTML and CSS, {m.js ?? '0 KB'} of JavaScript, no web fonts{m.images && <>, and up to {m.images} of lazy-loaded screenshots</>}.
    Measured from the build{m.measured && <> on {fmt(m.measured)}</>}, <a href="/notes/measured-not-claimed">not typed in</a>. No analytics.
  </p>
</Base>
